<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Afcol raises interim shr, div steady.</title>
<headline>Afcol raises interim shr, div steady.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended Sept 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     96.2	  vs  95.9</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 48.0	  vs  48.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   25.67	 vs  25.09</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   27.33	 vs  29.25</p>
<p>    Tax			  8.86	 vs  10.75</p>
<p>    Financing costs	  2.80	 vs   5.14</p>
<p>    Turnover		 564.03	 vs 538.17</p>
<p>Div payable Dec 31</p>
<p>on register Nov 29</p>
<p>Full name:Associated Furniture Companies Ltd (Afcol)</p>
<p>    Share of associates'   7.03	 vs  8.59</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said that indications hinted that a satisfactory level of trading could be expected in the December quarter and that should these sales materialise, an overall earnings increase for the year, inclusive of the profit on the sale of investments, is expected.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
